"Licensor" means the copyright holders entitled to grant rights in the Software.
"You" means the individual or legal entity exercising rights under this license.
"Internal Use" means use for your own operations, including a company's analysis
of its own networks, security and infrastructure. Employees and contractors may
operate the Software solely on your behalf for that purpose. It does not include
providing Software functionality, network analysis or monitoring to external
customers as a paid service.
"Commercial Offering" means a product or service supplied to third parties for
a fee or other commercial consideration that includes, embeds, bundles, resells
or exposes the Software or its functionality. This includes paid appliances,
software products, hosted APIs, SaaS, managed monitoring and paid customer
network-analysis services. An offering remains commercial if the Software is
advertised as a free component of a paid bundle. Merely using the Software to
secure or operate your own business infrastructure does not make your unrelated
products or services a Commercial Offering under this license.

